      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHAQ KEEPING (7) has been beaten for early speed lately, last time finishing fifth (24.95) in a NG at Goulburn. Solid record here at the distance winning two races. Safe beginner but wide box to overcome and will need some luck. Has ability and is a key runner. ZIPPING RUFFIAN (1) produced a modest effort most recently when seventh at this track over 622m behind Zulu Sharp (36.89) in a Grade 5. Was in the money the start prior. Reliable out of the boxes and should take advantage of the inside draw. Should be about the money. TARAWI BRUMBY (4) finds it hard to break through. Finished in the minors latest when second (29.80) at this track and may be close to breaking through. Has a good record here including two wins. Solid beginner who can clear the tricky draw. Expected to feature again. ZIPPER DAY (2) cannot be ruled out.",
